  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_5bf70bdb08af459db252f6b9f3d25915",
      "statement": "FrozenArmMixin implements ADR-0031 A1's \"register + dual-exclude\" convention: a frozen arm is a plain registered nn.Module submodule (so Lightning's automatic .to(device) owns its placement) that is kept off the optimizer (requires_grad=False plus the host's trainable-arm-only configure_optimizers) and off the checkpoint (the state_dict override), and is held in eval() across module.train().",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/adr/0031-device-ownership.md#L15-L31",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6c936f7ecda1f5e04f306da2dc6d1704b86756720d71f54312ac232d28277c78:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/modules/frozen_arm.py#L1-L11",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0797f01da74f2247b8300cd8ae07400087b077616bd3483065f0af7499b52aa3:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/modules/frozen_arm.py#L19-L42",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4b644d66afaefa441cfa06e86b11ec92ef095e54ff2536d4bb066b4a10f02a6f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_083d3659c18b4360b3a0892d04fd79d2",
      "statement": "_register_frozen_arm applies the uniform frozen-arm prep exactly once at construction (arm.eval(), requires_grad_(False) on its parameters, setattr registration as a normal submodule, and the arm-name set union), so a newly added frozen arm cannot forget the freeze; the arm-name set is a class-level frozenset default, so a host with no frozen arms degrades to a no-op rather than AttributeError.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/modules/frozen_arm.py#L44-L70",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1407d79d4fd5fec8b3548dbd7b2f0236bce9798013b20338bb3a91e60dbf8733:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f780ad4e536e48799391dc3fe4b776df",
      "statement": "The mixin's state_dict override strips the frozen arms by mutating the caller-supplied destination IN PLACE under the caller-supplied prefix, because the wrapper recursion (DDP's module.state_dict(destination=..., prefix='module.')) discards the child's return value and reads the shared destination — building a fresh dict would leave the multi-GB arms in the checkpoint.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/modules/frozen_arm.py#L82-L105",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:19414104e9bdf43116dce701b0afa36a6380b2553b09a125335ff357101a56ab:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://tests/test_frozen_arm_mixin.py#L77-L112",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c1f10ae3408683d3edfc54485836deb51caac57ba5305fffb6b6221264ce9f6c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1dcce3cdf0ac448eb5d853cb9c7f39cf",
      "statement": "load_state_dict is strict on the trainable keys with the frozen arms as an explicit allow-list: stray incoming frozen keys are stripped, the super() load runs with strict=False, and any missing or unexpected non-frozen key raises RuntimeError (no blanket strict=False, which would also hide a missing trainable key and resume on stale or random weights).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/modules/frozen_arm.py#L107-L137",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:01d618e345d65323ff4304bbfcc9aee0057c937522aafc8fdcbc847717b4cf43:"
